<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":37003,"e":37095,"k":"block","t":"Appearance tabKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#appearance-tab\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":37104,"e":37196,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000","f":["<img alt=\"Appearance settings tab\" src=\"../../assets/screenshots/settings/appearance.png\" />"]},{"s":37204,"e":37261,"k":"block","t":"Customize the application window and dialog visual style.","f":[]},{"s":37291,"e":37298,"k":"block","t":"Setting","f":[]},{"s":37308,"e":37312,"k":"block","t":"Type","f":[]},{"s":37322,"e":37328,"k":"block","t":"Values","f":[]},{"s":37338,"e":37345,"k":"block","t":"Default","f":[]},{"s":37355,"e":37364,"k":"block","t":"Stored as","f":[]},{"s":37402,"e":37412,"k":"block","t":"App Design","f":[]},{"s":37422,"e":37430,"k":"block","t":"dropdown","f":[]},{"s":37440,"e":37582,"k":"block","t":"Default, Matrix Terminal, Holographic Interface, Klingon Tactical, Elegant Dark, Amber CRT, Synthwave '84, Gruvbox Retro, Nord Arctic, Dracula","f":[]},{"s":37592,"e":37599,"k":"block","t":"Default","f":[]},{"s":37609,"e":37631,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000","f":["<code>appDesign</code>"]},{"s":37652,"e":37676,"k":"block","t":"Enable design animations","f":[]},{"s":37686,"e":37692,"k":"block","t":"toggle","f":[]},{"s":37702,"e":37709,"k":"block","t":"On, Off","f":[]},{"s":37719,"e":37721,"k":"block","t":"On","f":[]},{"s":37731,"e":37770,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000","f":["<code>appDesignAnimationsEnabled</code>"]},{"s":37791,"e":37803,"k":"block","t":"UI font size","f":[]},{"s":37813,"e":37819,"k":"block","t":"number","f":[]},{"s":37829,"e":37851,"k":"block","t":"80–160 % in steps of 5","f":[]},{"s":37876,"e":37907,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000","f":["<code>uiFontScalePercent</code>"]},{"s":37928,"e":37952,"k":"block","t":"Match display resolution","f":[]},{"s":37962,"e":37968,"k":"block","t":"toggle","f":[]},{"s":37978,"e":37985,"k":"block","t":"On, Off","f":[]},{"s":37995,"e":37998,"k":"block","t":"Off","f":[]},{"s":38008,"e":38036,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000","f":["<code>uiFontScaleAuto</code>"]},{"s":38057,"e":38075,"k":"block","t":"Chat color profile","f":[]},{"s":38085,"e":38093,"k":"block","t":"dropdown","f":[]},{"s":38103,"e":38205,"k":"block","t":"Automatic (theme), Original, Paper, Midnight, Cyberpunk, Retrowave, Forest, Ocean, Terminal, GPT, Cute","f":[]},{"s":38215,"e":38232,"k":"block","t":"Automatic (theme)","f":[]},{"s":38242,"e":38273,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000","f":["<code>chatColorProfileId</code>"]},{"s":38306,"e":38660,"k":"block","t":"The KTPH000 and KTPH001 buttons next to the dropdown step backward and forward through the designs (wrapping around at the ends). When a design other than KTPH002DefaultKTPH003 is selected, a preview image of that design is shown below the controls; the KTPH004DefaultKTPH005 design has no preview and shows a short note in its place.","f":["<code>◀</code>","<code>▶</code>","<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":38668,"e":38828,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Enable design animationsKTPH001 doubles as a reduce-motion switch: turning it off stops the animated design effects while leaving the colors in place.","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":38836,"e":39069,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Chat color profileKTPH001 themes the AI chat and swarm surfaces. The default KTPH002Automatic (theme)KTPH003 derives its palette from the active terminal theme's agent-panel colors; the other profiles are fixed palettes.","f":["<strong>","</strong>","<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":39132,"e":39136,"k":"block","t":"Note","f":[]},{"s":39144,"e":39338,"k":"block","t":"App Design applies only to korTTY's application windows and dialogs. Terminal sessions and the file editor retain their own independent color settings (configured via the Colors or Themes tabs).","f":[]},{"s":39372,"e":39460,"k":"block","t":"UI font sizeKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#ui-font-size\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":39469,"e":39955,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000UI font sizeKTPH001 scales korTTY's own interface — the menu bar and its dropdowns, dialogs, form labels, buttons, tab titles, the dashboard, the file browser and the status bar. It takes effect the moment you save; no restart is needed, and windows that are already open resize with it. The main window's first-launch size grows along with it, and dialogs that remember their size are re-measured after a change rather than reopening at a size that no longer fits their text.","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":39963,"e":40096,"k":"block","t":"It deliberately does KTPH000notKTPH001 touch surfaces that already have their own size control, so the two never fight each other:","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":40126,"e":40133,"k":"block","t":"Surface","f":[]},{"s":40143,"e":40172,"k":"block","t":"Where its size is set instead","f":[]},{"s":40210,"e":40227,"k":"block","t":"Terminal sessions","f":[]},{"s":40237,"e":40303,"k":"block","t":"The KTPH000FontKTPH001 tab, plus the View menu's zoom shortcuts","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":40324,"e":40335,"k":"block","t":"File editor","f":[]},{"s":40345,"e":40376,"k":"block","t":"The KTPH000EditorKTPH001 tab","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":40397,"e":40436,"k":"block","t":"AI chat, agent plan and activity panels","f":[]},{"s":40446,"e":40497,"k":"block","t":"Their own KTPH000 / KTPH001 buttons","f":["<code>A-</code>","<code>A+</code>"]},{"s":40518,"e":40538,"k":"block","t":"Session journal page","f":[]},{"s":40548,"e":40587,"k":"block","t":"The journal viewer's appearance popover","f":[]},{"s":40620,"e":40901,"k":"block","t":"Two further parts of the interface keep their size at every setting: the macOS application menu (the one in the system menu bar), because macOS draws it rather than korTTY, and the AI swarm status strip, whose labels are painted onto a canvas together with hand-computed positions.","f":[]},{"s":40909,"e":41175,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Match display resolutionKTPH001 derives the size from the primary display instead, and disables the number field while it is on. The value comes from the display's KTPH002logicalKTPH003 height — the resolution the operating system reports after its own scaling:","f":["<strong>","</strong>","<em>","</em>"]},{"s":41205,"e":41226,"k":"block","t":"Logical screen height","f":[]},{"s":41236,"e":41248,"k":"block","t":"UI font size","f":[]},{"s":41286,"e":41299,"k":"block","t":"Below 1400 px","f":[]},{"s":41335,"e":41347,"k":"block","t":"1400–1799 px","f":[]},{"s":41383,"e":41395,"k":"block","t":"1800–2299 px","f":[]},{"s":41431,"e":41448,"k":"block","t":"2300 px and above","f":[]},{"s":41496,"e":41794,"k":"block","t":"This is why a Retina MacBook stays at 100 %: macOS already scales it, so it reports roughly 1100 logical pixels and needs no help. The case the option exists for is a 4K or 5K display running at 100 % operating-system scaling, where korTTY really does get the full 2160 or 2880 pixels to draw into.","f":[]},{"s":41857,"e":41861,"k":"block","t":"Note","f":[]},{"s":41869,"e":42227,"k":"block","t":"Automatic is a suggestion, not a measurement. JavaFX cannot report a display's physical size, so korTTY cannot tell a 27-inch 4K panel from a 32-inch one at the same resolution, even though they need different sizes. If the result does not suit you, turn the option off and set the percentage yourself — your manual value is remembered while automatic is on.","f":[]},{"s":42242,"e":42608,"k":"block","t":"Automatic tops out at 140 % and the manual setting at 160 %. The ceiling is deliberate: a handful of dialogs size themselves from fixed pixel widths, and beyond that point their text starts to crowd. korTTY re-reads the display when you save the settings, so after changing your monitor setup, open Settings and save again (or restart) to pick up the new resolution.","f":[]},{"s":42631,"e":42711,"k":"block","t":"Font tabKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#font-tab\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":42720,"e":42800,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000","f":["<img alt=\"Font settings tab\" src=\"../../assets/screenshots/settings/font.png\" />"]},{"s":42808,"e":42854,"k":"block","t":"Set the terminal and editor typeface and size.","f":[]},{"s":42884,"e":42891,"k":"block","t":"Setting","f":[]},{"s":42901,"e":42905,"k":"block","t":"Type","f":[]},{"s":42915,"e":42921,"k":"block","t":"Values","f":[]},{"s":42931,"e":42938,"k":"block","t":"Default","f":[]},{"s":42948,"e":42957,"k":"block","t":"Stored as","f":[]},{"s":42995,"e":43006,"k":"block","t":"Font Family","f":[]},{"s":43016,"e":43024,"k":"block","t":"dropdown","f":[]},{"s":43034,"e":43123,"k":"block","t":"Common monospace fonts (Monaco, Courier New, Menlo, Fira Code, etc.) and all system fonts","f":[]},{"s":43133,"e":43143,"k":"block","t":"Monospaced","f":[]},{"s":43153,"e":43200,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000","f":["<code>defaultTerminalSettings.fontFamily</code>"]},{"s":43221,"e":43230,"k":"block","t":"Font Size","f":[]},{"s":43240,"e":43246,"k":"block","t":"number","f":[]},{"s":43256,"e":43263,"k":"block","t":"8–72 pt","f":[]},{"s":43285,"e":43330,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000","f":["<code>defaultTerminalSettings.fontSize</code>"]},{"s":43418,"e":43422,"k":"block","t":"Note","f":[]},{"s":43430,"e":43633,"k":"block","t":"The Font tab sets global defaults for all new terminal connections. Individual connections can override these values via their own connection settings. A live preview is shown as you adjust the controls.","f":[]},{"s":43665,"e":43749,"k":"block","t":"Themes tabKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#themes-tab\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":43758,"e":43842,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000","f":["<img alt=\"Themes settings tab\" src=\"../../assets/screenshots/settings/themes.png\" />"]},{"s":43850,"e":43990,"k":"block","t":"Create, edit, and manage terminal color themes. Themes define colors (text, background, cursor, ANSI) and styling for all terminal sessions.","f":[]},{"s":44021,"e":44117,"k":"block","t":"Theme managementKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#theme-management\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":44148,"e":44154,"k":"block","t":"Action","f":[]},{"s":44164,"e":44175,"k":"block","t":"Description","f":[]},{"s":44213,"e":44233,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000AddKTPH001","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":44243,"e":44274,"k":"block","t":"Create a new custom color theme","f":[]},{"s":44295,"e":44316,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000EditKTPH001","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":44326,"e":44455,"k":"block","t":"Modify the selected theme. The button stays enabled for built-in themes but does nothing when clicked — duplicate the theme first","f":[]},{"s":44476,"e":44502,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000DuplicateKTPH001","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":44512,"e":44557,"k":"block","t":"Copy the selected theme as a new custom theme","f":[]},{"s":44578,"e":44601,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000DeleteKTPH001","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":44611,"e":44668,"k":"block","t":"Remove a custom theme (built-in themes cannot be deleted)","f":[]},{"s":44721,"e":44811,"k":"block","t":"Theme optionsKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#theme-options\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":44842,"e":44849,"k":"block","t":"Setting","f":[]},{"s":44859,"e":44863,"k":"block","t":"Type","f":[]},{"s":44873,"e":44880,"k":"block","t":"Default","f":[]},{"s":44890,"e":44899,"k":"block","t":"Stored as","f":[]},{"s":44937,"e":45002,"k":"block","t":"When enabled, applying a theme also changes font family and size.","f":[]},{"s":45012,"e":45018,"k":"block","t":"toggle","f":[]},{"s":45028,"e":45031,"k":"block","t":"Off","f":[]},{"s":45041,"e":45069,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000","f":["<code>applyThemeFonts</code>"]},{"s":45157,"e":45161,"k":"block","t":"Note","f":[]},{"s":45169,"e":45363,"k":"block","t":"When this option is enabled, selecting a theme from the Colors tab's color profile dropdown will also apply that theme's font family and size. When disabled, only the theme's colors are applied.","f":[]},{"s":45410,"e":45525,"k":"block","t":"Built-in vs. custom themesKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#built-in-vs-custom-themes\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":45534,"e":45830,"k":"block","t":"korTTY includes a set of built-in color themes (e.g., Default, Dark Mode, Solarized Light). Built-in and custom themes are stored together in a single file, KTPH000. All themes appear in the Colors tab's color profile selector and in connection-specific theme dropdowns.","f":["<code>~/.kortty/themes.xml</code>"]},{"s":45896,"e":45903,"k":"block","t":"Warning","f":[]},{"s":45911,"e":46030,"k":"block","t":"Built-in themes cannot be edited or deleted. To modify a built-in theme, duplicate it first, then edit the custom copy.","f":[]},{"s":46065,"e":46155,"k":"block","t":"Theme previewKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#theme-preview\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":46164,"e":46390,"k":"block","t":"A live theme preview displays the theme's colors. The preview shows six swatches — foreground, background and cursor, plus the AI agent panel's background, run and error colors — so you can evaluate a theme before applying it.","f":[]},{"s":46426,"e":46532,"k":"block","t":"Cross-tab integrationKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#cross-tab-integration\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":46547,"e":46711,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Colors tabKTPH001: Choose a theme via the \"Color Profile\" dropdown; if the Themes tab's font option is enabled, the selected theme's font is also applied.","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":46721,"e":46902,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Connection settingsKTPH001: Each individual SSH connection can override the global font and theme via its own settings (accessible in Connection Manager or Quick Connect).","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":46912,"e":47113,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Terminal emulationKTPH001: Font and theme colors affect only the terminal content; the application UI style (menu bar, dialogs, tabs) is determined by the Appearance tab's app design setting.","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":47998,"e":48013,"k":"text","t":"\n  Back to top\n","f":[]},{"s":48256,"e":48297,"k":"text","t":"MIT-licensed · Developed by Daniel Mengel","f":[]},{"s":48343,"e":48355,"k":"text","t":"\n    korTTY ","f":[]},{"s":48363,"e":48370,"k":"text","t":"v2.10.0","f":[]}]}